remediation:
1. Implement Authentication Requirement:
   - Require users to log in before accessing any profile data
   - Validate session tokens on all profile requests
   - Redirect unauthenticated users to login page

2. Implement Authorization Checks:
   - Verify the requesting user is authenticated via session/JWT validation
   - Restrict users to only view their own profiles OR explicitly public profiles
   - Implement access control lists (ACL) for public profile access
   - Return 403 Forbidden for unauthorized access attempts

3. Code Example:
   ```javascript
   app.get('/profile/:id', (req, res) => {
     // Check if user is authenticated
     if (!req.session.userId) {
       return res.redirect('/login');
     }

     // Check if user can access this profile
     if (req.session.userId !== req.params.id) {
       return res.status(403).send('Access denied');
     }

     // Fetch and return profile data
     const user = getUserProfile(req.params.id);
     res.send(renderProfile(user));
   });
   ```

4. Additional Security Measures:
   - Use middleware to enforce authentication on all protected routes
   - Implement proper session management with secure cookies
   - Add comprehensive logging of profile access attempts
   - Implement rate limiting on profile endpoints to prevent enumeration
   - Consider using UUIDs instead of sequential IDs to reduce enumeration attacks
   - Validate user IDs are valid ObjectIds before querying database
